{"message":"My recommendation is the **Silver Plus Account**. It offers tiered APY of **3.0% to 4.5%**, and your Blue Account adds a **+0.35% APY boost**. It also includes built-in savings-goal tracking.

The maintenance-fee risk is limited: maintain at least **$2,500** to avoid the **$8 monthly fee**. Since you don’t yet know your deposit amount or withdrawal pattern, this is a safer growth option than Platinum, which requires $50,000 to avoid a $25 monthly fee. The fee-free Bronze Account avoids maintenance fees entirely but is less attractive if maximizing growth is your goal.

I can’t open the Silver Plus Account today because personal savings eligibility requires holding an active checking account for at least 14 days. Your Blue Account was opened on November 14, 2025, so you should become eligible on November 28, 2025, assuming your accounts remain in good standing. You’ll then have 30 days after opening the savings account to fund it, or it may be closed."}
